xnu 0464: ring the doorbell at three sizes

Measured 2026-11-26: the PBL consumes the doorbell and reads inside the 512 KiB
it is told about, yet BHI_STATUS never leaves 0, the fetched image writes no
warm entry, and lowering the max read request size to 128 bytes changes
nothing.

mondrianwifisizes=1 rings the same IOVA at 4 KiB, 64 KiB and 512 KiB with a
distinct session id each, reading BHI_STATUS and BHI_ERRCODE 500 ms after every
ring. Success for the small sizes and silence for the large one names a
size-dependent transfer; silence for all three names an ack that waits on
something other than the DMA.

